        "title_paragraph_spacing": 20,
        "title_paragraph_spacing_mob": 20,
        "paragraph": "<p>Luxe Sassy LLC (\"Luxe Sassy,\" \"we,\" \"our,\" or \"us\") values your privacy and is committed to safeguarding it by following this privacy policy (the \"Policy\").</p><p>This Policy explains what information we may gather from you, or that you may give us, when you visit the Site or shop our Products (both defined below). It also describes how we use and share that information and the choices available to you.</p><h2>Scope of the Policy</h2><p>This Policy covers information collected through our website, <a href=\"https://www.luxesassy.com\">https://www.luxesassy.com</a>, and any other website, product, or service that shows or links to this Policy (together, the \"Site\"), through which we sell fashion, jewelry, and related goods (the \"Products\"). It does not cover websites, apps, or online services that carry their own privacy policy or that do not show or link to this Policy.</p><h2>This Policy is Part of Our Terms of Service</h2><p>This Policy forms part of the <a href=\"https://www.luxesassy.com/policies/terms-of-service\">Terms of Service</a> that govern your use of the Site. Please take a moment to read both documents so you understand our practices and your responsibilities when browsing and buying from us. By using the Site, you agree to be bound by the Terms of Service and this Policy.</p><h2>Updates to this Policy</h2><p>We review our privacy practices periodically, and they may change. Please check this page from time to time to stay informed. Any information collected after the Effective Date shown above will be handled under the version of the Policy in force at that time. Whenever we revise this Policy, we will update the Effective Date at the top of this page.</p><h2>Information We Collect</h2><p>On some parts of the Site, we may ask you to share information that identifies you personally (\"Personal Information\"), and you may ask us to send you information. Besides what you choose to give us, the Site may also gather information about you and how you use it automatically.</p><h2>Information We Automatically Collect</h2><p>When you interact with the Site, we automatically gather information about that activity, including details about the device you use.</p><p>Cookies and Device Identifiers. A cookie is a small file stored on your device when you visit a website, which that website can later read. We use cookies, device identifiers, and similar technologies to gather information and power certain Site features. For example, we may use them to:</p><ul><li>see how visitors move through the Site (such as the pages they view, the links they click, and how long they spend on each page);<br/></li><li>make Site features work (such as remembering details you already entered or settings from earlier visits);<br/></li><li>tailor your experience on the Site; and<br/></li><li>strengthen our marketing, including targeted advertising.<br/></li></ul><p>We may use session cookies, which are deleted when you close your browser, and persistent cookies, which stay on your device for a longer period. Information gathered this way may not identify you directly, but we may connect it with Personal Information you give us. If you prefer not to receive cookies, you can set your browser to block them or to warn you before one is stored. Accepting cookies is not required to visit the Site, but some features may not work if your browser refuses them.</p><p>Information from Your Computer or Mobile Device. When you visit the Site on a computer or mobile device, we may automatically gather information from or about that device, such as your IP address, the dates and times of your visits, your general location (based on your IP address), and details about your hardware, software, and device. This helps us understand how you used the Site and other actions you took on it. We also automatically record log data whenever you access the Site.</p><h2>Information You Provide to Us</h2><p>Individual Information. We may collect information directly from people who buy or show interest in buying our Products, or who choose to create an account with us. This may include Personal Information.</p><p>Email Content and Newsletters. You may share Personal Information with us by emailing the address shown on the Site or by using a contact form. We use it to reply to you or complete your order, and we may also use it to tell you about products or offers we think you will like. If you join our email newsletter, you can unsubscribe whenever you wish. Any interests you share with us may be used for marketing and promotions, and you may receive occasional emails from us or a related business as a result.</p><p>Payment Information. To buy Products on the Site, you may provide payment details such as card or other financial account information. We use this only to complete the purchase you are making, and it may be handled by a third-party vendor for us. All payments for our Products are processed by a third-party payment processor.</p><p>Additional Sources of Information. You may give us more information when you ask about our Products, whether by email, through the Site, or by phone. We may combine this with information we receive through other ways you interact with us.</p><h2>How We Store Information</h2><p>We apply technical and organizational safeguards that provide security reasonable and appropriate to the risk posed to the Personal Information we hold. We rely on well-established vendors to help us deliver our services and Products. Even so, sending information over the internet always carries some risk, and while we take sensible steps to protect your Personal Information, we cannot guarantee its security. You send Personal Information through the Site at your own risk, and we are not responsible if anyone gets around our security measures.</p><h2>Third-Party Analytics Tools</h2><p>In addition to information you give us directly, we use analytics tools, including third-party services such as Google Analytics, to collect information that helps us understand how visitors use the Site. You can learn more about <a href=\"https://marketingplatform.google.com/about/analytics/\">Google Analytics</a> and about <a href=\"https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites\">how Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.</p><h2>Third-Party Advertising Tools</h2><p>Third parties may place cookies or other tracking tools, such as web beacons or pixels, on your computer or mobile device to follow your online activity across unrelated websites and show you targeted ads on those sites. For example, we use the Meta (Facebook) Pixel to learn more about who visits our Site and to show you relevant ads elsewhere online.</p><h2>How We Use Information</h2><p>We use the information we collect to sell you Products, improve your time on the Site, refine our product range, and support our marketing and promotions. More detail is set out below.</p><p>Use of Information You Provide to Us. In general, we may use the information you give us through the Site:</p><ul><li>to deliver the Product information and content you ask for;</li><li>for security and fraud-prevention purposes;</li><li>to give you effective customer service;</li><li>to personalize your experience on the Site;</li><li>to send you information and notices about your use of the Site;</li><li>to better understand your needs and interests;</li><li>to improve the content, features, and usability of the Site;</li><li>to improve our product range;</li><li>to improve our marketing and promotional efforts; and</li><li>for any other purpose described in a privacy notice, click-through agreement, or other agreement between you and us.<br/></li></ul><p>See \"Your Choices\" below for the options you have regarding how we use your information.</p><p>Use of Aggregated Information. We may combine information collected through the Site to build an overall picture of our audience and how visitors use the Site. We use this combined information to improve our content, run our services, deliver Products, and understand our audience as we create new Products and services. We may also share aggregated information that no longer identifies any individual with our service providers and potential advertisers so they can better understand or market to our audience.</p><h2>Third-Party Data Sharing and Disclosure</h2><p>Compliance with Law or Protection of Rights. We may disclose the information we collect, including Personal Information, when we believe in good faith that doing so is needed to comply with the law, a court order, or a subpoena. We may also disclose it to prevent or look into possible crimes such as fraud or identity theft, to protect the Site, to enforce our terms or other agreements, or to protect our rights or property or the rights, property, or safety of others.</p><p>Business Negotiations. From time to time we may consider selling, buying, merging, or otherwise restructuring our business. While negotiating such a deal with a third party, we may need to disclose your Personal Information. If so, we will take reasonable steps to protect it, such as requiring the other party to sign a non-disclosure agreement that limits how the information may be used and keeps it confidential.</p><p>Business Transfers. If we go through a merger, divestiture, change of control, restructuring, reorganization, dissolution, or sale or transfer of some or all of our assets, whether as an ongoing business or as part of bankruptcy, liquidation, or a similar process, the information you submit through the Site, including Personal Information, may be transferred to a partner, buyer, or other successor as part of the assets transferred.</p><p>Vendors. We may hire third-party vendors to help us run the Site and better serve our visitors and customers, including vendors that analyze collected information for marketing or similar purposes. Some of these vendors may use cookies to collect information for us, and each maintains its own confidentiality and security standards. We may also work with companies that provide payment, data management, order fulfillment, shipping, and promotional services, and we give them only the information they need to perform those services.</p><p>We may also share information, including Personal Information, with third-party vendors that help us offer and deliver our Products, such as suppliers who ship orders directly to you or a cloud provider that hosts our data. These vendors may access Personal Information only for a limited purpose and a limited time.</p><p>We do not disclose Personal Information to third parties for their own direct marketing.</p><h2>Links to Third-Party Websites</h2><p>The Site may link to other websites or resources that we do not control. These links do not mean Luxe Sassy endorses those websites. Luxe Sassy provides them only for your convenience and is not responsible for their content. Your use of any linked website is governed by that website's own terms of use and privacy policy.</p><h2>Your Choices</h2><p>In General. We respect your right to choose how your Personal Information is collected and used. For example, every newsletter or promotional email we send includes instructions for unsubscribing.</p><p>Unsubscribe from Newsletters or Promotional Communications. We aim to send you information you find useful. If you would like to be removed from our mailing lists at any time, follow the unsubscribe instructions in our messages or email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@luxesassy.com\">info@luxesassy.com</a>. Please include your full name and email address so we can locate you on our lists. Once we have what we need, we will remove you as requested. Please allow us a reasonable amount of time to process your request.</p><p>Opt-Out Links. We do not control how third parties use your information, but you can opt out of some third-party activities using the links below.</p><ul><li><br/>To opt out of Google Analytics, visit: <a href=\"https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout\">https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout</a><br/></li><li><br/>To opt out of certain advertising features, visit: <a href=\"https://youradchoices.com/control\">https://youradchoices.com/control</a><br/></li></ul><p>Do Not Track Mechanisms. Because technology keeps changing and the industry has not agreed on what Do Not Track signals mean, we do not currently guarantee that we will respond to them.</p><h2>Children's Privacy</h2><p>The Site is not meant for anyone under 16. Children under 16 may not use the Site or its content without written permission from a parent or guardian. If you believe a child under 16 has given us information through the Site without a parent's or guardian's consent and supervision, please contact us using the details below.</p><h2>Contact Us</h2><p>If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please email us at <a href=\"mailto:info@luxesassy.com\">info@luxesassy.com</a> or visit <a href=\"https://www.luxesassy.com\">https://www.luxesassy.com</a>.</p>",
